245	
246	HCL formatting rules observed:
247	
248	- Tables are emitted in creation order, then `schema "main" {\n}` last. No blank lines anywhere.
249	- Every column block always has `null` (explicit `true`/`false`) and `type`.
250	- `INTEGER PRIMARY KEY` (without AUTOINCREMENT) → `null = true`, plain `primary_key` block
251	  (see `posts.id`); `INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT` → `null = true` plus
252	  `auto_increment = true` (see `users.id`).
253	- SQLite UNIQUE constraints surface as indexes named after sqlite's autoindex
254	  (`sqlite_autoindex_<table>_<n>`), `unique = true`, `columns = [...]`.
255	- DEFAULTs: numeric literals unquoted (`default = 18`, `default = 1.5`); string literals quoted
256	  with embedded quotes unescaped (`default = "hello 'world'"`); `CURRENT_TIMESTAMP` →
257	  `default = sql("CURRENT_TIMESTAMP")`.
258	- CHECK constraint: `check "age_check" { expr = "(age >= 0)" }` — expression includes the
259	  original parentheses.
260	- Attribute alignment: `=` signs are aligned by padding within each block (gofmt-style, e.g.
261	  `null           = true` when the block also has `auto_increment`).
262	- Blocks inside a table appear in order: columns (definition order), `primary_key`,
263	  `foreign_key`s, `index`es, `check`s (see rich2 for FKs).
264	
265	## Rich schema #2: FKs with actions, indexes (unique/partial/expression/desc)
266	
267	Database DDL:
268	
269	```sql
270	PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;
271	CREATE TABLE parent (
272	  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
273	  code TEXT UNIQUE
274	);
275	CREATE TABLE child (
276	  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
277	  parent_id INTEGER REFERENCES parent(id) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE SET NULL,
278	  parent_code TEXT,
279	  FOREIGN KEY (parent_code) REFERENCES parent(code) ON DELETE SET DEFAULT
280	);
281	CREATE INDEX idx_child_pid ON child(parent_id);
282	CREATE UNIQUE INDEX idx_child_code ON child(parent_code);
283	CREATE INDEX idx_partial ON child(parent_id) WHERE parent_id > 10;
284	CREATE INDEX idx_expr ON child(parent_id + 1);
285	CREATE INDEX idx_desc ON child(id DESC);
286	```
287	
288	Command: `atlas schema inspect -u "sqlite://rich2.db"` — exit 0, stdout verbatim:
289	
290	```hcl
291	table "parent" {
292	  schema = schema.main
293	  column "id" {
294	    null = true
295	    type = integer
296	  }
297	  column "code" {
298	    null = true
299	    type = text
300	  }
301	  primary_key {
302	    columns = [column.id]
303	  }
304	  index "sqlite_autoindex_parent_1" {
305	    unique  = true
306	    columns = [column.code]
307	  }
308	}
309	table "child" {
310	  schema = schema.main
311	  column "id" {
312	    null = true
313	    type = integer
314	  }
315	  column "parent_id" {
316	    null = true
317	    type = integer
318	  }
319	  column "parent_code" {
320	    null = true
321	    type = text
322	  }
323	  primary_key {
324	    columns = [column.id]
325	  }
326	  foreign_key "0" {
327	    columns     = [column.parent_code]
328	    ref_columns = [table.parent.column.code]
329	    on_update   = NO_ACTION
330	    on_delete   = SET_DEFAULT
331	  }
332	  foreign_key "1" {
333	    columns     = [column.parent_id]
334	    ref_columns = [table.parent.column.id]
335	    on_update   = SET_NULL
336	    on_delete   = CASCADE
337	  }
338	  index "idx_child_pid" {
339	    columns = [column.parent_id]
340	  }
341	  index "idx_child_code" {
342	    unique  = true
343	    columns = [column.parent_code]
344	  }
345	  index "idx_partial" {
346	    columns = [column.parent_id]
347	    where   = "parent_id > 10"
348	  }
349	  index "idx_expr" {
350	    on {
351	      expr = "parent_id + 1"
352	    }
353	  }
354	  index "idx_desc" {
355	    on {
356	      desc   = true
357	      column = column.id
358	    }
359	  }
360	}
361	schema "main" {
362	}
363	```
364	
365	Notes:
366	
367	- FKs are **unnamed in sqlite**, so atlas names them `"0"`, `"1"` following sqlite's
368	  `PRAGMA foreign_key_list` ids (FK id 0 = the table-level `FOREIGN KEY` clause on
369	  `parent_code`, id 1 = the inline `REFERENCES` on `parent_id` — i.e. reverse of DDL order).
370	- `on_update`/`on_delete` are always emitted, unquoted enum-like values:
371	  `NO_ACTION`, `SET_DEFAULT`, `SET_NULL`, `CASCADE`.
372	- Partial index → `where = "parent_id > 10"`.
373	- Expression index → `on { expr = "parent_id + 1" }` (no `columns` attr).
374	- DESC column index → `on { desc = true\n column = column.id }` (attribute order: `desc`, then `column`).
375	
376	## Views and triggers — NOT emitted
377	
378	Database DDL:
379	
380	```sql
381	CREATE TABLE t1 (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, val TEXT);
382	CREATE VIEW v1 AS SELECT id, val FROM t1 WHERE id > 0;
383	CREATE TRIGGER trg1 AFTER INSERT ON t1 BEGIN UPDATE t1 SET val = NEW.val WHERE id = NEW.id; END;
384	CREATE VIEW v2(x, y) AS SELECT id, val FROM t1;
385	```
386	
387	`atlas schema inspect -u "sqlite://rich3.db"` (exit 0) prints **only the table** —
388	views and triggers are completely absent from the default HCL output, and also absent from
389	`{{ sql . }}`, `{{ json . }}`, and `{{ mermaid . }}` output:
